        "correct_option_index": 0,
        "feedback_fil": "Una: Ang pinagsamang childcare barrier at tanong tungkol sa iskedyul ay sapat para sa pagpaplano, kung walang detalyeng makakakilala sa pamilya. Ikalawa: Ang larawan ng household forms ay naglalantad ng hindi kailangang pribadong detalye; hindi iyon ang kailangan ng grupo. Ikatlo: Ang pangalan at opinyon ng kapitbahay ay hindi angkop; ang opinyon ay hindi ebidensya ng dahilan. Sa wakas, tinanggap ng chair ang pinagsamang buod at napagkasunduang itanong niya sa itinalagang health team member ang paraan ng paglilinaw sa iskedyul sa susunod na coordination meeting. Kinumpirma ni Gibs kung sino ang gagawa at paano kukunin ang sagot. Hiwalay niyang kinumpirma sa awtorisadong midwife ang pagtanggap ng indibidwal na ulat at kanilang follow-up. Walang ipinangakong appointment o childcare.",
        "feedback_en": "First: The aggregated childcare barrier and scheduling question are sufficient for planning if no details identify a household. Second: Photographs of household forms expose unnecessary private details; the group does not need them. Third: Names and a neighbor’s opinion are inappropriate; an opinion is not evidence of the cause. In the ending, the chair acknowledges the aggregated summary and agrees to ask the designated health team member how to clarify scheduling at the next coordination meeting. Gibs confirms who will act and how to obtain the response. Separately, he confirms that the authorized midwife received the individual report and checks their follow-up agreement. No appointment or childcare is promised."
      }
    }
